{
  "id": "T-27",
  "question": "Does a projectile's damage fall off along the same line?",
  "bible": "§11",
  "gameVersion": "44.1.4.1",
  "reports": [
    {
      "on": "2026-11-25",
      "words": "Arca Plasmor projectile doesn't register a hit at all above 30m. Also follows its linear falloff from 10-20m. Importantly, Fatal Acceleration on these weapons DOES increase the range of the projectile. Max rank makes it still hit at ~43m."
    },
    {
      "on": "2026-11-25",
      "words": "I meant it follows our rule. 600 damage up close, already at 18m down to 200, 17m 240, 16m 300, 12m 512. I saw a hit at 43."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Asked for with no mods, standing still, at the body of a level 200 Runner, and no numbers were predicted to Pavel. As in T-25, a waypoint of 16 m means more than 15 and up to 16 m: the cases use the middle of that metre, and the tolerance is half a metre of the line and half a point. 300 at 16 m and 240 at 17 m are at the near end of theirs; the projectile is 3 m thick. The wiki's line, down to 33.33% at 20 m, would show 360 to 400 at 16 m, 320 to 360 at 17 m and 280 to 320 at 18 m. A line that ends halfway would show 200 at 16 and 17 m. The range isn't replayed: no number was read off. The engine ends it at 42 m with Fatal Acceleration, as the wiki does, so the hit at 43 m is beyond it by up to a metre. Arca Plasmor is in the fixture because the library can't say yet that its head multiplier is 1x.",
